    <section>
        <h2>Things Learned</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>Displaying "Hello World" using simple coding.</li>
            <li>Understanding the basic request-response flow in Rails.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Request-Response Flow</h2>

        <p>
            Browser → Route → Controller Action → View → Response to Browser
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Key Takeaway</h2>

        <p>
            When a user visits a URL, Rails identifies the matching route,
            executes the corresponding controller action, renders a view,
            and sends the resulting response back to the browser.
        </p>
    </section>
